{"t":1378120.7805242,"req":"h01","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","loop","draft"],"answer":"The original attention mechanism divides the query\u2011key dot products by a constant (specifically \\(1/\\sqrt{d_k}\\)) before applying softmax to prevent the dot products from becoming too large when the dimensionality \\(d_k\\) is large. Large dot products push the softmax into regions with very small gradients, which hampers learning. Scaling the dot products keeps them in a range where the softmax has useful gradients and improves training stability. [C:attention:10]"}
