{"t":1378208.5523567,"req":"h07","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","draft"],"answer":"Moshi\u2019s Inner Monologue is a training and inference procedure that jointly models text and audio tokens. It first predicts time\u2011aligned text tokens as a prefix to the audio tokens, allowing the model to exploit the knowledge from the text modality while remaining a speech\u2011to\u2011speech system. This hierarchical semantic\u2011to\u2011acoustic token generation improves linguistic quality and enables streaming speech recognition and text\u2011to\u2011speech by simply adjusting the delay between text and audio tokens. [C:moshi:1] [C:moshi:19]"}
